sition, step-back abstraction, self-consistency-style comparison, ReAct-like loops, tree-style search, and bounded reflection. `prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/codex/CODEX_RUNTIME_GUIDE.md` makes the mapping explicit: Prompt Chaining / Planning belongs in base prompts, and `Appendix A / advanced prompting execution families` route to `PROMPT_search_reasoning_overlay`, with example-catalog references treated as structure-only. `prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/03_examples/PROMPT_example_catalog.md` contains matching exemplar entries for advanced prompting and prompt chaining, but also explicitly says the catalog does not become an advanced prompting policy owner or chaining owner, which prevents overstatement rather than creating an ownership gap. `prompt-stack/v32/harness/freezes/rg-2026-05-06-a/snapshot/prompt-stack/v32/codex/skills/grounded-research/SKILL.md` further reinforces the routed behavior with bounded decomposition, route comparison, selective reflection, and staged research loops. Because the active bundle itself provides the ownership and routing answer, no out-of-scope operator doc is required.","limitations":["This is a document-level parity verdict, not behavioral proof from replay or execution artifacts.","The bundle directly reflects the named advanced prompting families, but it does not establish one-to-one coverage of every possible Appendix A technique beyond the families explicitly listed.","The example catalog contributes structural exemplars only; policy ownership remains with the base prompt, search-reasoning overlay, and runtime guide."]}
